# The hyperbolic plane H^2, geodesic polar coordinates: ds^2 = dchi^2 +
# sinh(chi)^2 dphi^2. Direct hyperbolic analogue of the round 2-sphere
# (ds^2 = dtheta^2 + sin(theta)^2 dphi^2) -- exercises sinh AND cosh
# together (Christoffel symbols involve cosh(chi)/sinh(chi), same shape
# as the sphere's cos(theta)/sin(theta)), including the cosh^2-sinh^2=1
# identity during Ricci/Kretschmann's own simplification. Constant
# negative curvature: expected Ricci scalar -2 (Gaussian curvature -1,
# R = 2K in 2D) -- exact sign flip of the sphere's +2.
manifold H2 dim 2
bundle TH2 on H2 dim 2
chart polar on H2 coords (chi, phi)
metric g on polar bundle TH2 {
  [chi,chi] = 1,
  [phi,phi] = sinh(chi)^2
}
